

T-Creates is a personal crochet portfolio website created to showcase my handmade crochet creations and share my passion for crochet. The website allows visitors to learn about me, explore my projects, and find ways to contact me.

The website was developed using HTML5 and CSS3, with responsive design techniques to ensure it works on different screen sizes. Git and GitHub were used to manage the project files and support publishing the website online.

The website contains four pages: Home, About, Portfolio, and Contact. The Home page introduces T-Creates, the About page shares my story and goals, the Portfolio page displays my crochet projects, and the Contact page provides links to my email, WhatsApp, Facebook, and Instagram.

Features include simple navigation, responsive layouts, alternative text for images, an external CSS stylesheet, contact links, and comments in the code to improve readability.

Redesigning my website helped me improve my HTML and CSS skills and understand the importance of accessibility, organisation, and responsive design. One challenge was maintaining a consistent appearance across all four pages while ensuring the website worked well on smaller screens. Testing the website also taught me to check links and images carefully. Overall, this project increased my confidence in web development and allowed me to present my crochet creations in a professional and organised way.

